 # Preview Specifications
 
+## Core Behavior
+
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-001**: When a request identifies an unknown clip revision, the system SHALL return 404 without enqueuing a render job.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-002**: When the requested preview is cached, the system SHALL return 200 with the JPEG for the requested revision and renderer version.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
-- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
-- [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## 2Q Eviction Policy
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: The cache SHALL be logically divided into Queue A1 (new entries) with a limit of 4 GiB and Queue A2 (reused entries) with a limit of 8 GiB.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When a completed preview is admitted for the first time, the system SHALL place it in Queue A1.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When a cached entry in Queue A1 is accessed a second time, the system SHALL promote it to Queue A2.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: When promoting an entry to Queue A2 would exceed the 8 GiB A2 limit, the system SHALL evict entries from Queue A2 (least recently used first) to make space for the promoted entry.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: When Queue A1 exceeds its 4 GiB limit, the system SHALL evict entries from Queue A1 in FIFO order (earliest admitted first) until the limit is restored.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-015**: Eviction from either queue SHALL remove the cached JPEG data but SHALL NOT affect any pending render jobs, deduplication entries, or the pending-response protocol.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-016**: The queue-assignment state and size limits are private to the preview worker and SHALL NOT be exposed through any external API or client-accessible interface.
